  "story": {
    "headline": "Britain’s Andy Green sets another speed record, this time for fastest run in a hydrogen-powered car",
    "summary": "Green reached 653.908 kilometres per hour in a car powered by two hydrogen internal combustion engines with a combined 1,600 horsepower",
    "publisher": "Rally News",
    "url": "https://rally.news/categories/transportation/?article=Britain%E2%80%99s%2BAndy%2BGreen%2Bsets%2Banother%2Bspeed%2Brecord%2C%2Bthis%2Btime%2Bfor%2Bfastest%2Brun%2Bin%2Ba%2Bhydrogen-powered%2Bcar"
  },
  "researchBrief": "The story was corroborated across multiple sources, confirming that Andy Green set a new world land speed record for hydrogen-powered vehicles. The record speed of 406.320 mph (653.908 km/h) was achieved using a car powered by two hydrogen internal combustion engines with a combined 1,600 horsepower. The record was set at the Bonneville Salt Flats in Utah and is subject to official ratification by the Fédération Internationale de l’Automobile (FIA). The car, engineered by British construction equipment manufacturer JCB, also beat the previous hydrogen combustion world record of 185.5 mph (298.5 kph) set by the BMW H2R in 2004. The engines used in the car are adapted from those used in JCB’s heavy machinery and are part of the company’s £100 million hydrogen program. The record is significant as it exceeds the 303 mph hydrogen fuel cell mark, making the JCB Hydromax the fastest hydrogen-powered vehicle of any kind in history.",
  "sources": [
    "https://www.yourbigsky.com/news/national-news/ap-britains-andy-green-sets-another-speed-record-this-time-for-fastest-run-in-a-hydrogen-powered-car/",
